# Keep secrets and local state out of the build context.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .` into the builder stage. Without this file the
# local .env - which holds the Hedera operator key, Auth0 secrets and DB
# credentials - and the full .git history were copied into that layer, and the
# builder layer is exported to the GitHub Actions cache
# (cache-to: type=gha,mode=max in .github/workflows/deploy.yml).
#
# The final runner stage only copies .next/standalone, .next/static and public,
# so these never reached the published image - but they did reach the cache.

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# VCS
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Dependencies and build output (reinstalled/rebuilt inside the image)
node_modules
.next
out
coverage

# Local tooling and editor state
.vscode
.idea
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store

# Docs and test artefacts not needed to build
README.md
**/__tests__
jest.config.js
